{
  "id": "reduckAlertToPurchase",
  "name": "Alert to automatic purchase (Reduck)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Alert to automatic purchase\n\n### How it works\nFor buyers who chase restocks: when a back-in-stock alert reaches the webhook (for example from a bot that forwards a chat channel), this workflow reads the product page and checks the price and the stock. Then it reviews the checkout, and places the order only when the total is under your limit and the checkout did not change since the review. It posts **order placed** or **needs you**, with the reason, to your notification webhook.\n\nEach product is ordered once: the data table `alert_orders` keeps the products the workflow started to order, and a later alert for one of them stops. When your bank asks you to approve the payment in its app, the notification says so.\n\nThe scripts run in your own Chrome, signed in to Amazon.fr. Each alert uses up to 3 Reduck runs.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install `@reduck-ai/n8n-nodes-reduck` on n8n Cloud or self-hosted n8n: https://docs.reduck.ai/n8n/#quick-start\n2. In **Read Product**, create a **Credential** with your key from https://reduck.ai/api-keys.\n3. Install the Reduck extension. In that Chrome, sign in to Amazon.fr and keep Chrome open.\n4. In **Alert Webhook**, set a **Header Auth** credential.\n5. In **Config**, set:\n   - `max_price`: the most you pay for one item. Example: `80`\n   - `quantity`: how many items to order. Example: `1`\n   - `delivery_address`: optional, as Amazon lists it. Example: `Jane Doe, 12 rue de la Paix`\n   - `card_last4`: optional, the last 4 digits of the card. Example: `1234`\n   - `notify_webhook`: the URL that gets the result. Example: a Discord webhook URL\n6. Activate the workflow. This is not a test: an alert under your limits places a real order.\n\n### Customization\nTo use another shop, change the script addresses, their arguments and `product_pattern` in **Config**. Keep **Retry On Fail** off on **Place Order**.",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "4c988627-ddae-5703-ba0a-0c346b5b4784",
